course: dictionary
lesson: 12882
title: Caught up together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An entanglement is when things get twisted and caught together, like string in a knot. You can also use it for a tangle of problems or feelings. «The fishing net was an entanglement of rope, and the turtle could not swim free.» The net is twisted round the turtle and holds it fast, so entanglement means a tangle that traps something.
explain: The word comes from the verb entangle, which means to twist things together so they are hard to pull apart. «The kite got entangled in the tree.» The kite is caught in the branches and cannot fly. Entangle is the action, and entanglement is the tangle that results.
explain: Entanglement can also mean a difficult or confusing situation you are caught up in. «Sam wanted to stay out of the family's entanglements and just keep playing football.» Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "stay out of the messy problems between people" still fits, so you know you have it right.
fact: Entanglement means things twisted and caught together, like string, nets or wire.
fact: «Barbed-wire entanglements» are tangles of spiky wire that are hard to get through.
fact: Whales, turtles and birds can become caught in fishing nets and plastic, which is a sad kind of entanglement.
fact: A «romantic entanglement» is a love relationship that is complicated or confusing.
fact: In science, quantum entanglement is a strange link between tiny particles, studied by physicists.
exercise: «The fish was stuck in an entanglement of old nylon line.» What is the entanglement here? | A bright, shiny scale | A fast swim through the sea | *A tangle of line twisted and caught around the fish | A kind of fishing boat
exercise: «Mia was caught in a difficult entanglement with her two friends after the argument.» What does entanglement mean here? | A happy party | A piece of rope | A long walk home | *A messy, confusing situation between people
exercise: What does the verb entangle mean? | To count the stars | *To twist things together so they are caught | To shout loudly | To swim very fast
test: «Barbed-wire entanglements stopped the sheep from wandering.» Which word in the sentence names the tangled wire? | *entanglements | wandering | sheep | stopped
test: Which sentence uses entanglement in the science sense? | The entanglement of the crowd made us late. | Our cat had an entanglement with the wool basket. | *Scientists studied the strange entanglement between two tiny particles. | The hikers got an entanglement of ropes on the mountain.
exam: Which word is the verb form of entanglement? | enter | entrance | *entangle | entire
